          "hold": 50.0,
          "lines": [
            {
              "text": "One idea reshaped every tall building",
              "sub": "moving the strength to the outer walls",
              "size": "hook",
              "at": 0.0,
              "until": 6.58
            },
            {
              "text": "Dhaka, then Chicago, arriving in 1952",
              "sub": "an engineer named Fazlur Rahman Khan",
              "size": "h1",
              "at": 6.92,
              "until": 13.31
            },
            {
              "text": "The old way piles heavy steel inside",
              "size": "h1",
              "at": 13.65,
              "until": 17.26
            },
            {
              "text": "In 1969 the tube moves it outside",
              "size": "h1",
              "at": 17.6,
              "until": 21.01
            },
            {
              "text": "In 1973 nine tubes bundle like reeds",
              "sub": "nine columns tied together for strength",
              "size": "h1",
              "at": 21.35,
              "until": 27.93
            },
            {
              "text": "The outer skin grips the wind instead",
              "size": "h1",
              "at": 28.27,
              "until": 31.95
            },
            {
              "text": "Yet he warned against his own fame",
              "sub": "the engineer must not be lost in his tools",
              "size": "h1",
              "at": 32.29,
              "until": 39.08
            },
            {
              "text": "Nearly every supertall tower rests on it",
              "size": "h1",
              "at": 39.42,
              "until": 43.3
            },
            {
              "eyebrow": "Fazlur Rahman Khan, Chicago",
              "text": "The bundled tube reached the sky in 1973",
